  "body": "Follow-up to PR #3577 (issue #3567). The review of `d41c2b76a` on PR #3577 gave two notes. PR #3577 merged without pins for them.\n\nWhat the commit adds (commit `9d260b2f5`, branch named in the first comment):\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/level_ramp_entry.rs`, test `the_ramp_fallback_note_is_a_rings_fallback`: a new assert that `pass_start_fallbacks` counts the note of `StartSide::ramp_fallback_note` one time. Thus the operation names this fallback `FallbackCause::PassStart` (\"Pass starts at: ...\"), not \"Adaptive fell back to Offset rings\".\n- `crates/motion/tests/pass_start_engagement.rs`, new test `the_replaced_helix_entry_is_named_once_on_the_band_path`: on the band path with a Helix entry, the note \"... instead of the helix entry\" occurs exactly one time.\n\nReadings: the two tests pass locally (motion `pass_start_engagement` 7 of 7, motion lib `level_ramp_entry` 4 of 4). The first comment gives the result after the merge of the current `main`.\n\nNo code change. Only tests.\n\nDone means: a PR from the branch merges, and the two pins are on `main`.\n",
